            <ArticleTitle>Bilateral Achilles tendon rupture: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>220-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Bilateral Achilles tendon rupture is a rare injury. We present a case of a 59-year-old gentleman who sustained a bilateral Achilles tendon rupture when the tendon was subjected to normal physiological load. He was treated operatively with V-Y plasty and repair of the tendon with post-operative plaster immobilisation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
